  "storage_change": [
    "SparseArray<T> now owns a private TypedSparseStorage<T> containing the actual SparseArrayBase; BTreeMap and Option block storage and duplicate counts/capacity are removed.",
    "Ordinary T occupies native header/items/bitmap blocks directly, at native sizeof(T) stride. New inline-stride regression distinguishes this from the prior Option<T> representation.",
    "SetValue/Bind borrowed operations and Assign dispatch real raw engine callbacks. New clones publish only after success; existing slots use Clone::clone_from; native count/bit/destruction ordering remains authoritative.",
    "All iteration reads raw block bitmaps. Safe facade cursor ownership and captured exhaustion semantics remain intact. Legacy allocated-empty-block exhaustion remains capacity+increment.",
    "Private raw reserve_clone_table helper preserves retained table capacity for the existing Rust Clone extension, including removed and failed-construction blocks."
  ],
  "ownership_proof": [
    "Erased public SparseArrayBase remains !Send/!Sync. Only private typed owner implements Send for T:Send and Sync for T:Sync.",
    "Private Rc<UnsafeCell<State>> is never cloned or externally exposed as Rc; its strong count stays one. Moving typed owner cannot race reference-count operations. Shared access reads only; mutation requires exclusive typed owner borrow. Allocator is thread-safe. Destructor callbacks operate only on owned T.",
    "The private Rc allocation is retained because earlier Miri proved inline-state observer pointers become invalid during Drop &mut retag. Existing raw observer Drop regression passes in this batch.",
    "Typed owner drains live objects before raw field Drop. Base stored destructor is no-op because the private typed owner exclusively owns object lifetimes while raw base owns allocation bytes.",
    "Auto-traits preserve existing UnwindSafe/RefUnwindSafe bounds T:RefUnwindSafe and unconditional Unpin including PhantomPinned. Positive and negative trait tests plus threaded move, shared reads and scoped mutable iteration pass Miri.",
    "Mutable iterator explicitly preserves RefUnwindSafe for T:RefUnwindSafe, Unpin, Send for T:Send and Sync for T:Sync; exclusive borrow freezes metadata and each occupied slot is yielded at most once."
  ],
  "rust_extensions_and_boundaries": [
    "Zero-size T gets nonzero aligned stride; T aligned beyond usize header alignment gets a Box<T> pointer slot. Native ordinary object layout is unchanged; these Rust extensions are not credited as native declarations.",
    "Safe allocation entry points check block size, table bytes, capacity and address limits before raw allocation. Zero increment remains constructible for defined empty queries; indexed access panics.",
    "Panicking Rust destructors are caught inside non-unwinding native callbacks; engine cleanup completes, then first panic resumes. Multiple panics and panicking discarded panic payloads are drained without leaks. Native nonthrowing-destructor domain retains its callback timing.",
    "Owned SetValue, Clone, Clone::clone_from, Option lookup and standard borrowing iterators are existing Rust extensions. Clone first constructs a complete replacement and preserves source capacity; Clone::clone_from does not call native Assign, which reuses values and retains target capacity.",
    "Safe absent Option lookups check occupancy before raw get_value to avoid constructing/discarding a Failure and allocating its message.",
    "No binary ABI parity or identical global allocator-call count is claimed: the Rust raw engine retains private heap state for pointer provenance. Allocation topology and ordinary item placement match the raw engine native contract."
  ],
  "remaining_gaps": [
    "No global declaration inventory or mapping credit is changed; exact rustdoc binding, signature scope and downstream compiler proof remain coordinating-agent work.",
    "This migration does not add public inheritance/protected-field access to safe typed SparseArray; erased SparseArrayBase and generic BasicIterator remain separately available for unsafe derived-container adaptation.",
    "Native typedef/algorithm closure and all possible generic instantiations are not established by these finite runtime fixtures.",
    "Raw allocation exhaustion remains a Rust panic rather than a mapped Standard_OutOfMemory, as documented by the prior base-engine receipt."
  ],
  "inventory_credit": 0,
  "integration": "Coordinator merges into main, reruns relevant checks, then deletes worktree and merged branch. No PR and no archive."
